Z||000004||Oreif||12-05-2000||10:14 AM||||Just a word of caution on the 83 camero, GM didn't start putting 350's into the F-bodies until 1987. The earlier V-8's were 305's which were notorious for weak cams. So if it is a 350 it's not the original engine, or the person is selling it really doesn't know what engine it is.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-05-2000).]||||reg||4
